# React + TypeScript + Vite

This template offers an entry point for using React with Vite and Hot Module Replacement (HMR), along with some ESLint configurations.

At the moment, there are two officially supported plugins:

- [@vitejs/plugin-react](https://github.com/vitejs/vite-plugin-react/blob/main/packages/plugin-react) makes use of [Oxc](https://oxc.rs)
- [@vitejs/plugin-react-swc](https://github.com/vitejs/vite-plugin-react/blob/main/packages/plugin-react-swc) leverages [SWC](https://swc.rs/)

## React Compiler

The React Compiler is not enabled in this template due to performance concerns during development and builds. If you want to enable it, please refer to [this documentation](https://react.dev/learn/react-compiler/installation).

## Adding more to the ESLint configuration

In case you are building a production application, we suggest enhancing your configuration by enabling type-aware lint rules:

```js
export default defineConfig([
  globalIgnores(['dist']),
  {
    files: ['**/*.{ts,tsx}'],
    extends: [
      // Other configurations...

      // Replace tseslint.configs.recommended with the following
      tseslint.configs.recommendedTypeChecked,
      // As an alternative, use the following for stricter linting
      tseslint.configs.strictTypeChecked,
      // Optionally, use the following for styling guidelines
      tseslint.configs.stylisticTypeChecked,

      // Other configurations...
    ],
    languageOptions: {
      parserOptions: {
        project: ['./tsconfig.node.json', './tsconfig.app.json'],
        tsconfigRootDir: import.meta.dirname,
      },
      // other options...
    },
  },
])
```

Furthermore, you may install [eslint-plugin-react-x](https://github.com/Rel1cx/eslint-react/tree/main/packages/plugins/eslint-plugin-react-x) and [eslint-plugin-react-dom](https://github.com/Rel1cx/eslint-react/tree
